# One line ending in the repository, whatever the machine that wrote it uses.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary

# Except the mail. A message uses CRLF between its lines — that is in the
# format, not a Windows habit — and normalising it to LF produces files that
# are no longer what a mail client would export, which is exactly what these
# are here to be. Left exactly as they are.
#
# The reader copes with either, deliberately: a mailbox that has been through
# a text editor is a mailbox somebody will point this at.
*.eml -text
